    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The nurse working in a disaster shelter should expect to monitor physical and mental health of victims. Stress is common for all victims of a disaster due to displacement from homes, loss of possessions, loss of employment, fear of the future, and living closely with strangers. Signs of stress include headache, nausea, worry, fatigue, insomnia, irritability, nervousness, fear, and racing thoughts."
    }
   ],
